{"title":"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Another_way_to_find_a)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Another way to find a)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Alternate_solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternate solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Alternate_solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternate solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Another_alternate_solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Another alternate solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadtheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadtheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b4fd08c7f1e4d6d79c161a483417073efb9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003301fe7b911c3e98b9edb848283faa3917419e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a(\\log_a(\\log_a 2) + \\log_a 24 - 128) = 128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf9b03c88382c4e847395c392e6cbdfc57a05a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a(\\log_a x) = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first condition implies\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e141af144886175e8f888317b997783ed8351c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{128} = \\log_a\\log_a 2 + \\log_a 24 - 128\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf09086fc61ef1ac7826a4e494d7191da4210b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[128+a^{128} = \\log_a\\log_a 2^{24}\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d0629298cfc70e32f871a4c407d469282ea98a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{a^{128}a^{a^{128}}} = 2^{24}\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f23eccc1a1f771c12339626fa20390f60b1a790.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a^{a^{128}}\\right)^{\\left(a^{a^{128}}\\right)} = 2^{24} = 8^8\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b2f0ff53a64cfc9b0ec73ce13acef9d1800af3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{a^{128}} = 8$\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Putting each side to the power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aed56990dedba5a88a65e21245ccfd5d5e43ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f33b05e81a42b56c7513b809b3c9a4449181f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a^{128}\\right)^{\\left(a^{128}\\right)} = 8^{128} = 64^{64},\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/88537f4245eb91e9cf3c5a2bfebc9ad6cc3dede2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{128} = 64 \\implies a = 2^{\\frac{3}{64}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />. Specifically,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e1e08697b9e65cebdceeefef3bae90accc10c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_a(x) = \\frac{\\log_2(x)}{\\log_2(a)} = \\frac{64}{3}\\log_2(x)\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>so we have that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3447dd129730439d4db19b9f7f05fd503964b85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[256 = \\log_a(\\log_a(x)) = \\frac{64}{3}\\log_2\\left(\\frac{64}{3}\\log_2(x)\\right)\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55cc4782cbd511fe1cb8702814856a87505e0a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12 = \\log_2\\left(\\frac{64}{3}\\log_2(x)\\right)\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e031ac284a023d2bdafab29e41a312b4ad0093.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{12} = \\frac{64}{3}\\log_2(x)\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11da6c5f64d54c0fcf9012af6060fd6d91310927.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[192 = \\log_2(x)\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/256863c8c0cd4c0b9fc75e2ecc1c493d69c2b334.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 2^{192}\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We only wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fbdfd03a61851b13ccb48cd09f4c5bd49a01c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\bmod 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. To do this, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6bf0f50f77fa7dbb82d223e046c566068041cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\equiv 0\\bmod 8$\" width=\"97\" height=\"12\" /> and now, by the Chinese Remainder Theorem, wish only to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f5551945325ade93b40a9aa9ff5b8f7c3c5beb5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\bmod 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_Totient_Theorem\" title=\"Euler&#39;s Totient Theorem\">Euler's Totient Theorem</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8873102edbcf210b4457a0e3ba46e7daaa4ce2d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{\\phi(125)} = 2^{100} \\equiv 1\\bmod 125\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed2fd9516b24a348efdddd3db1d359e8ec46cd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{192} \\equiv \\frac{1}{2^8} \\equiv \\frac{1}{256} \\equiv \\frac{1}{6} \\bmod 125\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>so we only need to find the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb7859dca98e84b28d7416e236972591bb3932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\bmod 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. It is easy to realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e2b06a5142f0ae334be433cf5d25a18d24e022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 21 = 126 \\equiv 1\\bmod 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"196\" height=\"13\" />, so \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44dfd8d02e0ce83290b0d7ddaad6b4280ad5e4d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\equiv 21\\bmod 125, x\\equiv 0\\bmod 8.\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a>, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53ba037f36d57948f24065388153611351f8e67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\equiv \\boxed{896}\\bmod 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"156\" height=\"25\" />, finishing the solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Another_way_to_find_a.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Another_way_to_find_a)\">Solution 2 (Another way to find a)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Another way to find a)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/88486a4bc6c5b7ff13683acf4ce5d183d3b6cb52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_a(\\log_a(\\log_a 2) + \\log_a 24 - 128) = 128\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f8b1d4d50e889abf6ba40f3c423b68b7959ba2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\log_a(\\log_a 2))+\\log_a(24)=a^{128}+128\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75759472365ee01fcdd1813aefa762b7b4cb589c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\log_a(\\log_a 2^{24})=a^{128}+128\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe69f522e1133058eef4e7acc450e79ceb00a0b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2^{24}=a^{a^{(a^{128}+128)}}\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Obviously letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93bee1bf7b3372a967c061b823c5b3d0ce0b239a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> will simplify a lot and to make the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab79fb798cffdaf9fb5e3e2b60510c58bba09edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> term simpler, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc453143cd337cb9e1541b2b48476a8f8d9d44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^{\\frac{y}{128}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Then, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7df08776270d51c9db8073ab879aad27d96465f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{24}=2^{\\frac{y}{128} \\cdot 2^{\\frac{y}{128} \\cdot (2^y+128)}}=2^{\\frac{y}{128} \\cdot 2^{y \\cdot (2^{y-7}+1)}}\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8fe7460ba8c66b9c19f38655011c61258f1578c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 24=\\frac{y}{128} \\cdot 2^{y \\cdot (2^{y-7}+1)}\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/48346251b311595e12b7f5518f3a2a460d68ca92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 3 \\cdot 2^{10}=y \\cdot 2^{y \\cdot (2^{y-7}+1)}\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Testing, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> satisfy the equation so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c677f3f9302f74ed0921108d14d80a67e8240c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^{\\frac{3}{64}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbca7c9247ca8e9b51f936cbead0b47cfff8a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2^{192} \\equiv \\boxed{896} \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"229\" height=\"25\" /> ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_solution_1\">Alternate solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you've found <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> but you don't know that much number theory.\n</p><p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13fa1f8ff1ec6b9d51318c817f6f50f66645123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$192 = 3 * 2^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />, so what we can do is take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and keep squaring it (mod 1000).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a6657cec7e768518704e61ef95cb03c22362b65a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^3 = 8\\]\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b21c857a2c0adf26f52266853927ef0fb77caba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^6 = 8*8 = 64\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7ed13e540437d9443dc89f04342247e82f7c1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{12} = 64*64 \\equiv 96\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7ee7eca0328f6ce3fcf9e1007b7e1fdf80dd9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{24} \\equiv 96*96 \\equiv 216\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a16f0aa00c36777bd9bc42d0e02bc81ba2680aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{48} \\equiv 216*216 \\equiv 656\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65a2630e5a0d1850daecea50c789b7b632e007c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{96} \\equiv 656*656 \\equiv 336\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d52fd3a4529ef4c1f8dac0381cc90c733552cde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{192} \\equiv 336*336 \\equiv \\boxed{896}\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_solution_2\">Alternate solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87b6c3d2c7882bfafdfe2d7853612b7744aceab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\bmod 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> using modular arithmetic.\nIn the same way as solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can find that.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44dfd8d02e0ce83290b0d7ddaad6b4280ad5e4d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\equiv 21\\bmod 125, x\\equiv 0\\bmod 8.\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49cd49a93d784db7367e8cb18076a1190a8f4ebd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 8m = 125n+21\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" /> For some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\nTaking the equation mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c005904b3bbf3c9b300ba556b62e45183980e04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5n+5 \\equiv 0\\bmod 8\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165afb827b01502a624eeb698f72d01415df8672.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 7\\bmod 8\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486aceb5bda75641bdfdc44cc0a0806ffbfe65fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 8k-1\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" /> For some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\nPlug this back into the original equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/000b962f66975eadf57ede587bbfccc169fe6d99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8m = 125(8k-1)+21\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b348b543ef23798a179d3fdd3af984fe7505aee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8m = 1000k-104\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fa6b9d64477d6e46d12ba3993c67cf5423bac6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 8m = 1000k - 104\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b3c7bb9f0dab8fa6ddf83992111c6a522301d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\equiv -104 \\equiv 896\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40eb7a3294a3a1bac545f237ccacd2c80b827450.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\equiv 896\\bmod 1000\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>~sdfgfjh\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Another_alternate_solution_2\">Another alternate solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Another alternate solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can also just break down <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4e4a6a69fbb80176375172b5fd8898fcccd011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cbc2089e6272cb7540ccd7dbbfecc4688dcdfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> to the power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecfd3c2af3d08534bb6769a4383bdbddd7dc3779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^24=216 (mod 1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f469c9864702377a808da7389d4795effcb7a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216^8=896(mod 1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"21\" /> by some multiplication. so, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5121855c67142bc46660638eafc0eb0345d6f661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{896}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by mop 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/E-7YQ9ND5Ms\">https://youtu.be/E-7YQ9ND5Ms</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadtheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadtheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadtheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZVPhvjlBvWY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZVPhvjlBvWY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I\" title=\"2017 AIME I\">2017 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<t